Below is one patch that restores the proper padding on `<input type="search">` in Safari by forcing it to use the “textfield” appearance rather than its native search‐field rendering (which ignores padding). We add a universal `-webkit-appearance: textfield;` immediately after the `width: 100%` in `StyledTextInput`:

```javascript
### src/js/components/TextInput/StyledTextInput.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
  ${inputStyle}
  width: 100%;

  ${props => props.size && sizeStyle(props)}
=======
  ${inputStyle}
  width: 100%;
  -webkit-appearance: textfield;

  ${props => props.size && sizeStyle(props)}
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

With this in place, Safari will render the search input as a normal textfield (honoring padding) just like Chrome does.
